ically and callbacks route to the right phone, which matters far more at 100 seats than at 5."},{"keyTakeAways":"Pooled org-level numbers, billed separately from seats, replace the per-seat number sprawl that legacy dialers bill for."}],"blogName":"The best enterprise sales dialers in 2026"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/PszRRpX7tRBD6jXAw0QM4/c5f11b3f1061c8f5d73917893d605691/enterprise-sales-dialers-cover.webp","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"The best enterprise sales dialers in 2026"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"For most enterprise sales organizations the best dialer is Artisan, because it puts compliant calling inside one AI-run outbound platform, governed centrally rather than bolted on as a standalone tool. Teams whose entire motion is maximum-volume call-floor dialing should still look at dedicated parallel dialers like Nooks or Orum, which specialize in high-volume parallel calling.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"That answer only holds if you evaluate a dialer the way a VP of Sales or a RevOps lead actually has to: not on raw line count, but on whether it enforces compliance per lead, whether admins can govern it centrally, and whether the per-seat cost stays sane when you multiply it across a hundred reps. This guide ranks the field on those terms.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Comparison table","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Dialer","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Best for","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"con